description:
Ideal candidate for the Category Manager position:
Strong strategic procurement background, with proven experience in category management, strategic sourcing, supplier negotiations and contract management;
Specific category experience in Commercial Data, Insights & Analytics, Market Research, Competitive Intelligence, Forecasting and related professional/data services;
Pharma/Life Sciences industry experience – ideally with exposure to commercial functions and their specific procurement needs;
Understanding of the supplier landscape within these categories, including data providers, market intelligence and analytics service providers;
Strong stakeholder management skills, with the ability to engage senior business stakeholders, challenge requirements constructively and operate independently;
Commercial and analytical mindset, with experience developing sourcing strategies, evaluating complex service proposals, negotiating commercial models and driving value beyond savings;
Ability to operate in a managed services environment, demonstrating ownership, adaptability and a proactive, solutions-oriented approach.
Key Responsibilities:
Category Management:
Manage higher-impact or more complex COE categories (e.g., Facilities, Fleet, I&T, MRO, Office Supplies, PPE, Travel etc.) with distributed spend and multi-stakeholder influence;
Lead the development, maintenance, and execution of category strategies and sourcing plans across a portfolio of COE-designated categories;
Conduct spend analysis, opportunity assessments, and project prioritization across COE categories;
Monitor category performance, supplier dynamics, and compliance levels, recommending strategic improvements.
Sourcing Execution:
Lead end-to-end sourcing activities – including market analysis, RFx development, supplier evaluations, negotiations, and recommendation presentations;
Ensure sourcing events follow client policies, governance frameworks, and documentation standards;
Drive supplier base optimization, increase compliance, and enhance value delivery;
Partner with cross-functional and cross-regional teams to ensure consistent delivery of COE services.
Qualifications and Experience:
Bachelors Degree or equivalent work experience is required, MBA preferred;
8–12+ years of experience in procurement, category management, sourcing execution, or procurement consulting; COE or managed services experience preferred;
Proven ability to independently develop and execute category strategies for high-impact or complex categories;
Advanced negotiation skills, including multi-round commercial discussions and complex supplier interactions;
Experience mentoring junior team members or contributing to COE capability-building initiatives;
Strong analytical capabilities, including spend analysis, supplier assessments, and opportunity identification;
Excellent communication, stakeholder management, and influencing skills;
Expertise in an Indirect procurement category is preferred, such as HR, IT, Marketing, Travel, Facilities, MRO, Professional Services, or other related categories;
Strong ability to influence cross-functional stakeholders and drive adoption of category strategies.
Skills & Competencies:
Business and commercial acumen;
Strategic project management;
Stakeholder engagement & influencing;
Structured problem-solving and decision-making;
Supplier relationship management;
Results orientation and accountability;
Adaptability and leadership in a multi-client, multi-category environment;
Seeks to influence and manage collaboration across WNS/Procurement as a way to increase performance / productivity and spur innovation.
WNS, part of Capgemini, is an Agentic AI-powered leader in intelligent operations and transformation, serving more than 700 clients across 10 industries, including Banking and Financial Services, Healthcare, Insurance, Shipping and Logistics, and Travel and Hospitality. We bring together deep domain excellence - WNS’ core differentiator - with AI-powered platforms and analytics to help businesses innovate, scale, adapt and build resilience in a world defined by disruption.Our purpose is clear: to enable lasting business value by designing intelligent, human-led solutions that deliver sustainable outcomes and a differentiated impact. With three global headquarters across four continents, operations in 13 countries, 65 delivery centers and more than 66,000 employees, WNS combines scale, expertise and execution to create meaningful, measurable impact.
